The seven files under src/vendor/supabase/ui/lib/, src/vendor/supabase/ui/hooks/ and
src/vendor/supabase/ui/shadow-scroll-area.tsx are internal support modules the eighteen named
components import (a tab-index helper, size-variant constants, the mobile-breakpoint hook, the
horizontal-scroll hook, and the shadow-scrolling table container); they are vendored from the same
commit for the same reason as the components themselves and are not part of the console's own
source.


-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The files under src/components/ui/ come from shadcn/ui (https://ui.shadcn.com),
MIT licensed, added with `npx shadcn@latest add` against the `radix-nova` style
declared in web/components.json. They build on Radix UI primitives, also MIT.

**These are NOT the Supabase files above, and the separation is deliberate.**
The batch plan expected `npx shadcn@latest add` to yield Supabase's packages/ui.
Measured, it yields canonical shadcn/ui: every file in the Supabase section above
carries a `Vendored from supabase/supabase ... commit 6ac0316` header, single
quotes and Supabase's own helpers such as getExplicitTabIndex, while the CLI
output carries none of those and uses shadcn's `data-slot` convention. Listing CLI
output under the Supabase attribution would name the wrong upstream for a
differently-licensed component, which is an attribution defect rather than a
formatting one.

