`chart` was added by `M14-W388` and REMOVED by `M14-W392`, with `recharts`
dropped from package.json alongside it. It was the only importer of recharts,
while this console's dashboards are built on echarts -- four modules use it and it
already has a jsdom stub. Two charting libraries is weight for no gain, so the
console has one, and it is echarts. A shadcn chart is an echarts decision first if
it is ever wanted.

`sonner` was added by `M14-W388` and REMOVED alongside `skeleton.tsx`, with `sonner`
and `next-themes` dropped from package.json. Nothing imported `Toaster`, it was the
only importer of either package, and its spin utility compiled a keyframe into the
production stylesheet. The utility is deliberately not spelled here: Tailwind scans
every non-gitignored file in the project, so naming it in this note put the keyframe
straight back into the bundle -- measured, in the commit that removed it. It was kept for a named upcoming consumer, which
`CLAUDE.md` rules out: an abstraction for an anticipated second caller is debt with
no asset behind it.

`resizable` is kept for now, and is the sole importer of `react-resizable-panels`
which nothing else reaches. It carries the same speculative justification and
retires with the rest of the unreachable catalog.

`form` was requested and is absent: `npx shadcn@latest add form` reports success
and creates nothing, twice, with no error. `toggle` was not requested and is
present: the CLI added it as a dependency of `toggle-group`.

One note against the Supabase carve-out's section 6 -- no component may assert a
claim our data cannot support. `chart.tsx` is a container and tooltip wrapper
rather than a chart: it ships no gauge or ring of its own. Its class list does
style `recharts-radial-bar-background-sector`, so a CALLER could compose a radial
gauge with it. A bar chart over real counts is permitted; a gauge or health ring
is not, and that constraint lives at the call site because this file cannot
enforce it.

